aut he says it's nice to see you  again friend  she responds the pleasure's all mine and  as their handshake is being broadcast  worldwide on tv  jsc is celebrating but we see that it's  playing to tvs and  empty rooms everyone's sheltering  because of the air raid  it really underlines the severity of the  situation and how  important it was that they decided to go  forward with this that they made this  decision  and that nasa did back them up president  reagan sees the broadcast on air force  one and calls helen  she starts to apologize for letting it  happen but it turns out that he loved it  because he thought it was inspirational  he thinks there may still be a way to  get out of this situation  and asks about pathfinder and boron but  they're still out of communication range  there baron tells pathfinder they have  two minutes to comply with the blockade  and that's not something that they can  do according to their mission  we get an idea of the strategy they get  a radar lock on baron  from there the plan is to wait for them  to missile lock sea dragon  and then in the mere seconds they have  fire their missiles at the soviet  shuttle as i said earlier the stakes  here are that if they do that  on earth the soviets will launch a  nuclear attack on the southern us  then the u.s will fire their missiles  from western europe  attacking the soviet union and that'll  be that  so here's the thing the setup has it so  that ed is angry he can't make sense out  of what's going on in his marriage  and here he feels like there is a clear  right answer  he needs to follow orders he needs to  complete his mission  as we're watching this it isn't even 100  clear if he understands the chain  reaction of events that are gonna happen  if he does that sally ride does see this  though  and she points out that ed's the  commander of this mission he has the  final say  this is a call back to what happened  with apollo 10.  she brings up his testifying about this  in front of congress  and when he tells her to lock their  weapon system on boron she refuses the  order  he leaves his seat to relieve her from  her post and he's going to do it himself  until she pulls her gun and puts it to  his head  and orders him to step away from the  console and you couldn't ask for a more  tense situation  piscotty tries to talk them down he  throws out the idea that maybe there's a  way that they can not  let buron shoot down sea dragon but also  not shoot them down either but we're in  a ticking clock situation and they get  the alert that barron has target lock's  sea dragon  in an instant edd fires the missiles but  we learn that he's aimed them at sea  dragon instead of buron  and thus makes the only move that he had  available to him to try to  avert the crisis there's this amazing  shot where the two shuttles pass by each  other and they make eye contact  and the look on everyone's faces show  how close they came to starting world  war 3.  it's so perfect because the soviets  don't even really know what happened  they know they had their orders  i'm sure they went through hell they  were in their own intense situation  about whether they should follow through  with their orders or not  and all anyone knows at the end is  things would have turned out a lot  differently  if they were the ones who had fired on  sea dragon  pathfinder clears the moon and they're  contacted by houston  allen asks if they shot down barron and  everyone is relieved to find out they  didn't  ed doesn't know what to make of it he  doesn't know what to think because he  did just shoot down sea dragon he was  about to tell them that  but he has no idea what happened while  they were out of contact  it turns out that reagan diverted air  force one to moscow after signing a  treaty  to pull back forces on earth and in  space within dropoff  he says he was inspired by the images of  the apollo soyuz mission  and that was enough for him to reach out  his hand in peace  on tv we 