ween ed and  karen  it's on the back burner at this point  with everything else that's happening  and through kelly's reading of her  application to the naval academy where  she talks about how this  one thing that happened her being on the  crashed first flight of operation baby  lift which is a real thing that happened  in our timeline  how that shaped the story of her life  she talks about the idea of always  thinking that things happen for a reason  and while all of this will likely be  important for her character going  forward  she says am i doing what i'm supposed to  be doing falling in my father's  footsteps  it also works really well to tie up the  season  and drive home what they were trying to  do the question that the show asked is  what if what if things happened a little  differently what would that look like  just as kelly wonders what would have  happened if she wouldn't have been on  that flight  the show is based off this idea of what  if sergey korolev  lived what if he was able to fix the  problems that the soviets were having  with their rockets  and what if they were able to put a man  on the moon first  we see the ripple effects in this  timeline from that happening  we see the changes in technology we see  the changes in  competition to try to do the next thing  in space  and in season two we saw the darker side  the conflict that comes with that  she ends her story with a great quote  from john lennon saying  everything will be okay in the end if  it's not okay  it's not the end and it turns out that  her story was not the end of the season  because we see margot get a call from  sergey as she's walking through the  graveyard he pays his respects for gordo  and tracy  saying that they were heroes for america  and the soviet union  and the whole world and that is true in  their mission apollo soyuz  with dany's decision to reach out to the  cosmonauts and go through with it  anyways played a big part  in what happened as well that's not the 